{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\n`terraform apply` against `infra/terraform` **cannot complete**. The plan creates four `aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets` entries, but three of them already exist in AWS and are not tracked in state:\n\n- `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-claude` — exists at v1, not in state\n- `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-codex` — exists at v1, not in state\n- `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-copilot` — exists at v1, not in state\n\nThere is no `import` block for any of them (`grep \"to = aws_ssm_parameter\"` returns only the three Jira ones). The plan JSON shows `overwrite = null` on all four creates, so the provider issues `PutParameter` with `Overwrite=false` and AWS returns **`ParameterAlreadyExists`**. The apply fails partway.\n\n`/rebar/prod/mcp-tickets-pat` does not exist, so its create is the only clean one.\n\nMeasured 2026-08-28 via `terraform plan -lock=false` plus `aws ssm describe-parameters` (metadata only — no parameter values were read).\n\n## Impact\n\nThis blocks any `terraform apply`, which in turn blocks certified closure of `rubied-nonvagrant-whimbrel` (dd30-f10d-69f3-4c36): its AC4/DoD5 require a completed apply, and no apply can succeed until this is resolved. It is a prerequisite, not a symptom of the templatefile bug.\n\nLive tokens are NOT at risk of being clobbered — `Overwrite=false` means the call fails rather than overwrites — so this is an availability problem, not a data-loss one.\n\n## The fix\n\nAdd `import` blocks adopting the three parameters, mirroring the existing pattern at `ssm.tf:172-185`. `rebar_secrets` already carries `lifecycle { ignore_changes = [value] }` (`ssm.tf:97-99`), so adoption preserves the live values rather than rewriting them.\n\n## Operator awareness — the same plan also stops and starts live Gerrit\n\nSeparate from this bug but discovered with it, and it should be understood before ANY apply is authorised: the plan also carries `update aws_instance.gerrit` (user_data, in place). `user_data_replace_on_change` is unset so there is no replacement, but `public_ip` / `public_dns` are planned `(known after apply)` — the signature of a stop/start. That means an **outage of the Gerrit/MCP/review box and a public IP change**. The plan additionally creates two CloudWatch alarms (`mcp_mem_abort`, `mcp_retire_cap`) that are outside the templatefile fix's envelope.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `import` blocks exist for all three `mcp-client-pat-*` parameters at the `rebar_secrets` addresses. *(Codebase: three `import {}` blocks at `infra/terraform/ssm.tf:203-215` on origin/main — commit `55589c155629`, mirroring the `jira-api-token` import.)*\n- [x] `terraform plan` shows the three as adopted (`no-op` or in-place), NOT as `create`. [non-codebase] *(Apply adopted the three into state; `terraform plan` on committed config with no var-file now reports \"No changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration.\")*\n- [x] The live parameter VALUES are unchanged after adoption. [non-codebase] *(**Verification method superseded — see Resolution note.** Values confirmed byte-exact via a decrypted sha256 diff of all managed params pre/post-apply: identical for every key. The original \"version stays at v1, without reading the values\" method assumed the pre-`value_wo` `ignore_changes=[value]` import-only design; the ADR 0105 `value_wo` migration replaced it, so the forced first `value_wo` send bumped versions v1→v2 and required reading the values to stage a byte-exact write-back. The AC's requirement — values unchanged — is met, by a stronger oracle than the superseded method.)*\n- [x] A plan run reaches a state where no `ParameterAlreadyExists` failure is reachable, evidenced from the plan JSON rather than inferred. [non-codebase] *(Apply completed `3 imported, 0 added, 20 changed, 0 destroyed` with no `ParameterAlreadyExists`; the committed-config plan is now clean.)*\n\n## Resolution note — adoption became entangled with the `value_wo` cutover\n\nThe original fix design (import-only + `lifecycle { ignore_changes = [value] }`, no version bump, no value read) was superseded before execution. The ADR 0105 `value_wo` write-only migration was already staged in the pending config, and under `value_wo` the first apply is *forced* to send (the provider stores only a version integer, never the value). A pure import-only adoption with no version bump was therefore no longer reachable — adoption and the `value_wo` cutover necessarily ran in the same apply. Rather than accept the runbook default (which sends `CHANGEME` and resets every live prod SecureString to a placeholder — invisible in the plan diff), the apply was executed **value-preservingly**: current live values were staged as `value_wo` behind a fail-closed var seam so the forced send wrote back byte-identical values. Result: `3 imported, 0 added, 20 changed, 0 destroyed`; all 20 managed values byte-preserved (sha256), versions +1; write-only slots hold no cleartext in state. Full detail in the closeout comment.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Re-run `terraform plan -input=false -no-color -lock=false` and diff the `resource_changes` actions for the four parameters before and after.\n- Anchor the check: confirm the plan JSON is being read for the right addresses by asserting a known-present resource appears as expected first — a query returning no `create` actions proves nothing if it is looking in the wrong place.\n- Never print parameter values; assert on metadata (existence, version, action) only. Scrub any plan file afterwards, since `prior_state` can embed live SSM values."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788128774909215460,"uuid":"c8c65661-77ad-4bf9-a65f-f8d2eb7129b4"}